From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 11:13:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep computed calc trees correct and panic-free

A unit multiplier can only fold through a node when that node supports
product distribution. Keep the product around min(), max(), and clamp()
so computed serialization preserves the required 1 * term form.

A NaN wins min() or max() only when the NaN branches have compatible
units. Keep the function when relative and absolute units cannot be
reduced to one leaf.

Computed calc trees can contain empty sums, incompatible dimensions, or
final numeric leaves. Treat them as safe fallback values so layout does
not repeatedly unwind or crash the worker.

Empty sums simplify to numeric zero before construction. Keep the
existing conversion to a length without a debug-only panic, so malformed
trees stay recoverable in all build profiles.
